.TH GPUBENCH 1 "September 2026" "GPUBench 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpubench \- Modern cross-backend GPU compute and hardware ray tracing benchmark
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpubench
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GPUBench
is a high-performance cross-backend GPU compute and ray tracing benchmarking utility supporting Vulkan 1.4, AMD ROCm/HIP, and OpenCL 3.0. It evaluates raw compute capabilities (FP64, FP32, DualIssue, LDS, Indirect, FP16, BF16, FP8, FP6, FP4, INT8, INT4, 2:4 Structured Sparsity, Cooperative Vector), VRAM, cache, and PCIe/ReBAR/P2P interconnect bandwidth/latency, Async Compute & Copy Engine concurrency, GPU Work Graphs, hardware-accelerated BVH traversal (including Opacity Micromaps), dynamic wavefront ray scheduling via Device-Generated Commands (DGC), and Empirical Roofline modeling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Display program version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-benchmark\fR, \fB\-\-benchmarks\fR \fIBENCHMARKS\fR
Comma-separated list of benchmarks to run (e.g., fp32,fp64,dualissue,lds,indirect,fp16,bf16,fp8,fp6,fp4,int8,int4,sparsematrix,coopvector,membw,interconnect,l0b,l1b,l2b,l3b,cachebw,l0_cache,cache_latency_curve,asyncoverlap,workgraphs,pixelfill,rayrawtraversal,rayasbuild,rayintersect,rayanyhit,rayomm,rayprocedural,raypayload,rayscheduling,raydivergence,sysmembw,sysmemlatency,all).
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-group\fR, \fB\-\-groups\fR \fIGROUPS\fR
Benchmark groups to run: compute, memory, scheduling, graphics (combines raster & raytracing), raster, raytracing, system, or all.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR, \fB\-\-list\-benchmarks\fR
List all available benchmarks organized by group.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-groups\fR
List available benchmark groups.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR \fIINDEX\fR
Specify target GPU device index (e.g., 0, 1).
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\-devices\fR
List all detected GPU compute devices across backends.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-backends\fR
List available compute backends.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-backend\fR \fIBACKEND\fR
Specify compute backend: auto, vulkan, opencl, rocm (default: auto).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIINDEX\fR
Run only specific sub-test configuration index(es) within a multi-configuration benchmark.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-scene\fR \fISCENE\fR
Ray tracing scenario: showroom, indoor, outdoor, forest, all (default: all).
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-resolution\fR \fIRESPRESET\fR
Resolution preset: auto (scales dynamically by GPU VRAM capacity: 720p < 6 GB, 1080p < 10 GB, 1440p < 16 GB, 4K >= 16 GB), 720p, 1080p, 1440p, 4k, 8k, 1024x1024, or custom WxH (default: 4k).
.TP
\fB\-\-bounces\fR \fIBOUNCES\fR
Number of light bounces for multi-bounce path tracing (1..8, default: 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-spp\fR \fISPP\fR
Number of samples per pixel for path tracing accumulation (default: 1).
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-renders\fR, \fB\-\-dump\fR
Dump rendered images and parity difference heatmaps to the \fIrenders/\fR directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-dump\-renders\fR, \fB\-\-no\-dump\fR
Disable dumping rendered images to disk.
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-geometry\fR
Export procedural ray tracing scene geometry to Wavefront OBJ files.
.TP
\fB\-\-verify\-parity\fR
Enforce strict Megakernel vs. DGC framebuffer visual parity verification (PSNR >= 45 dB) and return a non-zero exit code on failure.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-snapshot\fR
Run in single-frame deterministic profiling snapshot mode for RGP / Nsight capture.
.TP
\fB\-\-rra\fR
Enable Radeon Raytracing Analyzer (RRA) BVH capture mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-isa\fR \fITARGET\fR
Disassemble compiled hardware shader/kernel ISA, VGPR/SGPR/LDS footprint, and instruction histograms via \fIVK_KHR_pipeline_executable_properties\fR or ROCm \fIllvm-objdump\fR without running benchmark loops. Combine with \fB\-\-full\-isa\fR to emit complete assembly.
.TP
\fB\-\-roofline\fR
Compute and display the Empirical Roofline analysis (peak memory/cache bandwidth ceilings, peak vector/matrix compute ceilings, ridge points, arithmetic intensity, and bottleneck classification) and include it in exported v2.0 JSON reports.
.TP
\fB\-\-power\fR
Display per-workload GPU package power and energy efficiency metrics (GFLOPS/W, GB/s/W, MRays/J).
.TP
\fB\-\-telemetry\fR
Display hardware compiler resource usage (VGPR/SGPR/LDS) and hardware performance counters where available.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Force execution even if concurrent GPU load or high GTT usage is detected.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational banners and progress output.
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Enforce strict execution hygiene: abort with a non-zero exit code if active background GPU contention is detected (override with \fB\-f\fR/\fB\-\-force\fR). Numerical validation failures always return a non-zero exit code regardless of \fB\-\-strict\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose logging output.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable Vulkan validation layers and detailed debug logging output.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\-json\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
Write benchmark results to a unified v2.0 JSON report file (compatible with both \fBgpubench \-\-import\fR/\fB\-\-compare\fR and \fBgpubench-gui\fR). Specify \fB\-\fR to direct pure JSON to standard output.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output pure JSON report directly to standard output (equivalent to \fB\-o \-\fR).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-import\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR \fIFILE\fR...
Load and display results from one or more unified v2.0 or v1.x benchmark JSON report files.
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\fR \fIFILE1\fR \fIFILE2\fR [\fIFILE3\fR...]
Compare benchmark JSON report files side-by-side with cross-device win tallies and relative performance deltas.
